From: openwrt-sonic-fullcone contributors
Date: Wed, 9 Apr 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] firewall4: add SONiC fullcone NAT with per-zone and
 per-protocol granularity

Adds fullcone NAT support to firewall4 with three levels of control:

  1. Global default:  config defaults / option fullcone 1
  2. Per-zone:        config zone / option fullcone 1
  3. Per-protocol:    config zone / list fullcone_proto udp

defaults.fullcone is a global gate. When off, all fullcone is disabled.
When on, each zone must explicitly set fullcone=1 to activate.
fullcone6 can be used to override the IPv6 setting independently.

The srcnat fullcone rules are emitted inside the masq4_src_subnets /
masq4_dest_subnets loops and carry the same saddr/daddr matches as the
regular masquerade rules, so masq_src/masq_dest keep applying.  The
dstnat fullcone rules are emitted after the chain-append user includes
so they cannot shadow user supplied dstnat rules; they still come after
the zone redirects.

The fullcone expression availability is probed once per boot and a
positive result is cached in /var/run/fw4-fullcone.

Requires the kernel fullcone expression (985/986 patches) and the
libnftnl/nftables userspace patches.
